        {
          "name": "quartech_designatedregistrantname",
          "label": "Designated Registrant Name",
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "name": "quartech_designatedregistrantphonenumber",
          "label": "Designated Registrant Phone Number",
          "format": "phoneNumber",
          "required": true,
          "validation": {
            "type": "length",
            "value": 14,
            "comparison": "equalTo",
            "postfix": "digits",
            "overrideDisplayValue": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "quartech_legalnamefirst",
          "label": "First Name",
          "additionalTextAboveField": "<p>Please note, Ministry of Agriculture and Food (AF) program staff may reach out to the primary contact throughout the work period to check in, and offer educational opportunities. For a participating practice to be eligible for reimbursement at the end of the work placement, the following documents must be received by the AF program administrator from each practice; end of program data collection, and and program evaluation forms. It is the practice’s responsibility to make sure these are submitted.</p>",
          "required": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "EligibilityStep",
      "displayName": "Practice",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "quartech_vetpracticeaccreditedbycvbc",
          "label": "Does your veterinary practice offer food animal services?",
          "required": true,
          "additionalTextAboveField": "<p>To be eligible for the program, applicants must meet the following eligibility requirements:<ul><li>Veterinary practice accredited by the College of Veterinarians of BC (CVBC) to provide food animal services.</li><li>Actively offering food animal services to clients during the work placement period. For this program, food animals are defined as animals raised to produce food or fiber, and include cattle, swine, sheep, goats, poultry, bison, and fish.</li><li>Practices that provide services to clients at any production scale (e.g. large-scale, small lot) are eligible.</li></ul></p>"
        },
        {
          "name": "quartech_numberoffulltimeveterinarians",
          "label": "Number of full-time (equivalent) veterinarians",
          "format": "number",
          "required": true,
          "validation": {
            "type": "numeric",
            "value": "0",
            "comparison": "greaterThanOrEqualTo"
          }
        },
